<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;HMS DUKE OF YORK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HMS Duke of York is a King George V-class battleship of the Royal Navy, commissioned in 1940, and played a significant role in World War II, particularly in key battles and legal filings."&lt;SEP&gt;"HMS Duke of York is a battleship commissioned during World War II, part of the King George V-class battleships."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROYAL NAVY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Royal Navy is the branch of the British Armed Forces responsible for naval operations, including the construction and operation of the King George V-class Battleships."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Royal Navy is the maritime arm of the British Armed Forces, and HMS Duke of York is part of its fleet."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KING GEORGE V-CLASS BATTLESHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"King George V-class battleship is a class of battleships, of which HMS Duke of York is a member, known for their role in World War II."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIRTH OF CLYDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Firth of Clyde is a sea inlet in Scotland where HMS Duke of York was anchored in 1942."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE CROWN VS. MCTAVISH SHIPPING CO.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Crown vs. McTavish Shipping Co. is a legal case involving allegations of negligence and breach of contract related to the transportation of war materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REAR ADMIRAL SIR REGINALD HALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rear Admiral Sir Reginald Hall led the internal investigation into the HMS Duke of York filing incident."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HALL REPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Hall Report is the internal investigation report into the HMS Duke of York filing incident, published in 1943."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOURNAL OF MARITIME LAW AND COMMERCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Journal of Maritime Law and Commerce is a publication that analyzed the implications of the HMS Duke of York filing and its impact on maritime law."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOHN BROWN &amp; COMPANY SHIPYARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"John Brown &amp; Company shipyard in Clydebank, Scotland, is where HMS Duke of York was commissioned in 1942."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE TIMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Times is a British national daily newspaper that reported on the commissioning ceremony of HMS Duke of York in 1942."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Times is a British newspaper that reported on the commissioning of HMS Duke of York."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANGUS KONSTAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Angus Konstam is an author who provided a detailed account of the HMS Duke of York's history, including its commissioning."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALAN RAVEN AND JOHN ROBERTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alan Raven and John Roberts are authors who provided a comprehensive history of British battleships during World War II, including HMS Duke of York."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEBRUARY 10, 1942&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"February 10, 1942 is the date when HMS Duke of York was served with a writ of summons in the legal case 'The Crown vs. McTavish Shipping Co.'"</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEBRUARY 4, 1942&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"February 4, 1942 is the date when HMS Duke of York was commissioned at the John Brown &amp; Company shipyard in Clydebank, Scotland."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD WAR II&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"World War II is the historical context in which HMS Duke of York and the King George V-class Battleships operated."&lt;SEP&gt;"World War II is the historical context in which HMS Duke of York operated and participated in various battles and legal filings."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AXIS POWERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Axis powers refer to the coalition of countries that fought against the Allies during World War II, and HMS Duke of York played a role in the battle against them."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLIED WAR EFFORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Allied war effort refers to the collective military and strategic efforts of the Allied nations, including the Royal Navy and HMS Duke of York, during World War II."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATERIAL WITNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Material witness refers to the role of HMS Duke of York in the legal case 'The Crown vs. McTavish Shipping Co.' as a key source of evidence."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAIN OF CUSTODY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chain of custody refers to the process of documenting the handling and transfer of evidence, which was crucial in the legal case involving HMS Duke of York."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liability refers to the legal responsibility determined in the legal case 'The Crown vs. McTavish Shipping Co.'"</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMUNICATION ERRORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Communication errors refer to the procedural issues highlighted in the Hall Report that contributed to the legal dispute involving HMS Duke of York."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KING GEORGE V-CLASS BATTLESHIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"King George V-class Battleships are a class of battleships, including HMS Duke of York, built for the Royal Navy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KONSTAM, A.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. Konstam is an author who wrote about the King George V-class Battleships."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAVEN, A.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. Raven is an author who co-wrote about British Battleships of World War Two."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROBERTS, J.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"J. Roberts is an author who co-wrote about British Battleships of World War Two."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSPREY PUBLISHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osprey Publishing is the publisher of A. Konstam's book on King George V-class Battleships."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARMS AND ARMOUR PRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arms and Armour Press is the publisher of A. Raven and J. Roberts' book on British Battleships of World War Two."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH BATTLESHIPS OF WORLD WAR TWO&quot;">
      <data key="d2">cb-0189</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. Raven co-wrote about British Battleships of World War Two, contributing to the understanding of these ships."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;HMS DUKE OF YORK&quot;" target="&quot;THE CROWN VS. MCTAVISH SHIPPING CO.&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"HMS Duke of York was involved in the legal case 'The Crown vs. McTavish Shipping Co.' as a material witness, with its logs and crew testimony being crucial in the case."</data>
      <data key="d5">"legal involvement, material witness"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0189</data>
    </edge>
